\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From a wavefunction to phase and translation measurements}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The positive wavefunction of \ref{fdip-00H6} assigns a position
probability density to a complete spatial configuration. For the
coupled chain of \ref{fdip-00GV}, multiplying a wavefunction by a
coordinate records a site value, while shifting that coordinate
compares two nearby configurations. A phase multiplication has
modulus one, and a coordinate shift preserves Lebesgue volume.
How do these operations express bounded quantum measurements and
their time correlations for the Hamiltonian already constructed?}
